-- the arguments of a primitive the compiled code reads: a load (cprim 768..1023) its byte string and
-- offset, a store (1024..1279) those and the value, a length (1280..1535) the byte string; the length
-- each carries last is the reflected semantics' bound, not computed (x-prim). Every other: all
x-prim-reads : Word → Lst Code → Lst Code
x-prim-reads p as =
  if andB (%wlt #767 p) (%wlt p #1536)
    then lc-take (if %wlt p #1024 then #2 else (if %wlt p #1280 then #3 else #1)) as
    else as
